# Build context exclusions for the backoffice image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The Dockerfile runs `bun install --frozen-lockfile` and then `COPY . .`.
# Without this file that COPY overwrites the clean install with whatever sits in
# the developer's working tree — 488 MB of host-built `node_modules`, plus a
# stale `.nuxt` cache, shipped into the build context on every single build.
# `api/.dockerignore` documents where that already cost this project a boot
# crash loop; the two Nuxt apps simply never got the same treatment.
#
# Scope note: this does NOT fix the arm64 `bun run generate` failure in this
# image. That was investigated separately and is a toolchain issue, not a
# context issue — the build fails identically with a clean context. Claiming
# otherwise here would send the next person down the wrong path.
#
# It also keeps `.env` and `.git` OUT of the image. This app's API base is baked
# into the bundle at build time from a build ARG; a local `.env` in the context
# could silently win over it, which is exactly the failure that sent production
# logins to http://localhost:8000.

# ── Secrets and local configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Version control and CI metadata ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# ── Dependencies: installed inside the image, never copied from the host ────
node_modules

# ── Generated output and caches: rebuilt in the image, never inherited ──────
.nuxt
.output
dist
.data
.cache

# ── Test artefacts: never part of a runtime image ───────────────────────────
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report
.playwright

# ── Editor and OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# ── Docker's own files: changing them must not invalidate the build context ─
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
